---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const seo = {
  title: "Colophon",
  description: "How this website is built",
};
---

<Page seo={seo}>
  <h1>Colophon</h1>

  <p>This is how my website is made. Updated everytime I remember to.</p>

  <h2>Build</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Framework:</strong> <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank">Astro</a>, generating plain static HTML;
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting:</strong> <a href="https://www.netlify.com" target="_blank">Netlify</a> on the free tier;
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/lsfgrd/lauro.xyz" target="_blank">public on GitHub</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Design</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Body font:</strong> <a href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Libre+Franklin" target="_blank">Libre Franklin</a> (self-hosted through Fontsource);
    </li>
    <li><strong>Interface font:</strong> whatever monospace font your system has;</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Social images:</strong> generated with <a href="https://github.com/vercel/satori" target="_blank">Satori</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics:</strong> <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com" target="_blank">GoatCounter</a>, privacy-focused, open source web analytics.
      It does not uses cookies and doesn't track you across sites. I just want to know how many people landed here.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <hr>

  <p>You also might be interested in my <a href="/ai">stance on AI</a>.</p>
</Page>
